From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Retain EUMM original attribution for the build-call wrapper

Preserve the exact original EUMM author/license text from fixed official7.34.
The observed boundary is an analogous API calling pattern, not a claim that
the parser implementation or earliest source version was copied. Add only
notice text; all original files and tests remain unchanged.
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (local packaging license preservation)

--- /dev/null
+++ b/BUILD-HELPER-LICENSE
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+Build-helper attribution and original license terms
+
+Makefile.PL labels its parse_args wrapper "copied from EUMM". The actual
+wrapper calls the EUMM API and passes shell-split PERL_MM_OPT plus ARGV; it
+does not embed EUMM's parser implementation. The analogous calling pattern
+is present in this fixed official ExtUtils-MakeMaker 7.34 source:
+https://cpan.metacpan.org/authors/id/B/BI/BINGOS/ExtUtils-MakeMaker-7.34.tar.gz
+SHA-256: 95f1eb44de480d00b28d031b574ec868f7aeeee199eb5abe5666f6bcbbf68480
+
+This records a concrete reference matching the distribution's declared EUMM
+generation version, not a claim about the first copied version or byte-identical
+parser code. The original EUMM AUTHORS and LICENSE text is preserved below;
+POD notation is retained. This is attribution, not a newly invented grant.
+
